#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#Note: This example works only with 32-bit LabView.
#
#This example is similar to Simulink: Radar Active Cruise: First Car (Ext. Sen.) and Second Car Ext. Sen.) except it is done in LabView.
#
#To run this example, follow the steps below.
#1.  Live animator is not used with this example.  Make sure set it to 0. First click the "Send to LabVIEW" button from this screen.
#
#2. This will open LabView Front Panel and load i-i_ACC.vi.  Change the "Car 1 Simfile" and "Car 2 Simfile" paths on the bottom of the panel.  The easiest way to find your CarSim database path is to go to Help > About CarSim from your CarSim Window. File >Save in the Front Panel to save this new paths in i_i_ACC.vi. Leave the LabVIEW Front Panel open.
#
#3. Then go to the linked dataset for the second car, "Radar Active Cruise: Second Car (Ext. Sen.)" Click the “Send to LabVIEW” button. Wait for a couple of seconds and click Run (the white arrow icon on the top) in the LabVIEW Front Panel.
#
#4. After the run, you can look at the results from CarSim (for example, using Plot, Video, etc.)
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

LOG_ENTRY Used Dataset: CarSim Run Control; { Simulink and LabVIEW Models } * LabVIEW Radar Active Cruise: First Car
